  "description": "AJILE12 is a long-term naturalistic electrocorticography (ECoG) dataset recorded opportunistically from 12 participants during clinical epilepsy monitoring at Harborview Medical Center, with 55 full-day recordings sampled at 500 Hz. It includes visually validated wrist-movement initiation events and coarse behavioural state labels (e.g., sleep/rest, TV, talking, eating) derived from simultaneous video. This iEEG-BIDS representation converts the original DANDI 000055 NWB release without altering signal values, and retains the original NWB files, including pose trajectories, in sourcedata.",
  "methods_description": "ECoG (grids, strips and some depth electrodes) was recorded during clinical monitoring, with simultaneous video used to estimate upper-body pose, detect wrist-movement events and annotate coarse behaviours. The authors applied median DC removal, 1-200 Hz band-pass, 60 Hz notch, downsampling from 1 kHz to 500 Hz and common-median re-referencing per electrode group. Electrodes were localised with FieldTrip using co-registered MRI and CT and warped to MNI space. Conversion to BrainVision float32 preserved the NWB values byte-for-byte, with event clock offsets verified per file.",
